    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n22291" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">incendĭārĭus</span></b> ,
			a, um, adj.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>causing a conflagration</i>, <i>setting on
			fire</i>, <i>fire-.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Adj.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">avis,</span>”
				<i>fire-bird</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					10, 13, 17, § 36</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">oleum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Veg. Mil. 4, 8</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">18</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tela,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Amm. 20, 11</span></i>
			. — </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">incendĭārĭus</span></b> ,
			ii, m., <i>an
			incendiary</i>, <i><span class="en">Tac. A. 15, 67</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Suet.
				Vit. 17</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">incendiarii, qui consulto incendium inferunt,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Paul. Sent. 5, 3, 6</span></i>
			.</div>
